# Scripts that run on Linux (VM batteries, build) or under node must keep LF
# line endings regardless of the checkout's core.autocrlf. A CRLF shebang/line
# breaks bash ("$'\r': command not found") and python on the VM.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Ledgers stay in the repo (evidence, full history) but out of `git archive`
# (ADR-0076 phase 2): only the 49 files the tools/l1 tests and scorers read
# ship. `**/*.*` matches files, not directories (no l1-raw directory name has
# a dot); `l1-raw/**` would prune whole directories and the re-includes below
# would never apply. A new test that reads a ledger adds its file here.
raptorpath/docs/l1-raw/**/*.* export-ignore
